# B0 (STOP): build the SHIP image tp4-ship-1 from this branch's pushed commit with the ship candidate baked as the image's serving default (ENV QWEN_C2_PROFILE) and
# THATCH_SERVING_SESSION_CAP baked as its max-num-seqs (8). REFUSED by c2_serving_job.read_bake while the profile's owner_traffic_waiver decision is not APPROVED: the owner
# approves first, the approval is committed (the decision sentence starts with APPROVED), and the tag is pushed on THAT commit (docs/tp4-ship-ln-w2-er.md). READ: 'baking the
# serving default c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-traffic with a session cap of 8', the provenance report '(c) the image default is the BAKED profile ...', no
# problem line, the image id. Measured basis: the tp4-er-1 build of this branch's parent took 34 minutes.
# TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the ship pack (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over that file on a throwaway commit of the approved branch head and
# push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Names no rig, card, host or registry. ORDER.txt has the order, the stop rules, the minutes and the pass rule.
